          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: The witness observes, from a 4th-floor terrace, a red object resembling a bell, seemingly equipped with portholes, moving at a constant speed and direction. Only one statement is collected. This statement lacks information. The free statement is concise, and key questions about the sky position are answered with a question mark. The direction of movement is not indicated, but the constant trajectory may suggest a non-luminous light object (plastic or fabric) carried by the wind, even if it appears as a \"bell with portholes around it.\" This case is classified C due to lack of information.",
